# Windsurf rules — SPaaS MDP flattener harness

This repo is a local proof of concept: Kafka -> Flink (DataStream flattener) -> Iceberg on
S3 (MinIO plus a REST catalog) -> Trino. It flattens nested manufacturing test events into
one flat row per event. All data is synthetic.

## Read these first
- RUNBOOK.md : exactly how to run and test (start here for any run or test task).
- README.md : architecture and quick start.
- NOTES.md : per milestone build log with verification output.
- context.txt : short project overview, accomplishments, and learnings.

## The test gate (run before and after every change)
- Fast: `bash scripts/test.sh` (JUnit in Docker, no host Gradle). Expect BUILD SUCCESSFUL
  and 29 passing tests.
- Full: `bash scripts/test.sh integration` (Testcontainers, slow). Expect
  `[IT] FINAL flattened=7 quarantine=2 audit=1`.

## Hard rules (do not break)
- Keep the two transform contracts: deterministic output, and never throw on a bad record
  (bad input becomes a quarantine record, never a crash).
- Do not change the version matrix (`processor/versions.gradle`, `docker/.env`), the docker
  compose stack, or the Kafka, Iceberg, or Trino wiring.
- Keep the Java package `com.example` (a privacy scrub; this repo is public).
- Scope is the manufacturing flattener only. No generic plugin system or transform registry.
- Work incrementally: one change, update its test, run `bash scripts/test.sh` to green.

## Notes
- Builds and tests run inside Docker (`gradle:8.10-jdk17`); you do not need host Gradle or a JDK.
- `make submit-job` is detached (`flink run -d`); it returns immediately and the job keeps
  running, so do not wait on it.
- A single `make freshness` burst is one commit window sample; the honest freshness claim is
  P95 under 10 seconds, bounded by the 5 second commit interval (`runtime.checkpoint_ms`).
